// You can specify that multiple data icons on the diagram
// actually refer to the same semantic data element, by
// continuing on the next line with `&`, `S&` or `O&`. The
// difference is that `&` keeps the same icon as the previous
// one, while the latter override it.
// While there is no visual difference, it is essential
// for the PE-BPMD extension, and maybe for future analysis
// modules as well. Further, it might help you to document
// the relationship between those data elements.
OD Data <-p1s ->p1e
// This is semantically the same data as the previous one,
// and it inherits the icon from the previous data element.
 & Data (the same) <-p2s ->p2e
// Again, semantically the same, but overriding the icon.
S& Data (still the same) <-p3s ->p3e

MF <-p1e ->p2s
MF <-p2e ->p3s
